    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Perched on an elevated one-acre site in the breathtaking coastal landscape of Carhoo, Dunquin, this is far more than a home—it is a lifestyle reserved for the fortunate few. With panoramic Atlantic Ocean views stretching towards the iconic Blasket Islands and, on clear days, the world-renowned UNESCO World Heritage Site of Skellig Michael, this exceptional property enjoys one of the most spectacular settings along the Wild Atlantic Way.\r\n\r\nDesigned with remarkable flexibility in mind, the residence currently presents as two self-contained living spaces beneath one roof, seamlessly connected by an internal doorway. Whether you envision a substantial family home, multi-generational living, guest accommodation, an income-generating opportunity, or a combination of home and business, the possibilities are as impressive as the views themselves.\r\n\r\nSet amid generous grounds extending to approximately one acre, the property offers exceptional privacy, extensive parking and a substantial steel garage, providing abundant space for vehicles, boats, hobbies, workshops or outdoor pursuits. Every aspect of the property has been thoughtfully positioned to embrace the surrounding landscape while offering the practicality and versatility that today’s discerning purchaser seeks.\r\n\r\nNestled in the heart of the Dingle Peninsula’s Gaeltacht, this is a location where dramatic scenery, rich Irish heritage and world-famous landmarks combine to create something truly extraordinary. From spectacular sunsets over the Atlantic to nearby cliff walks, pristine beaches and the vibrant culture of Dingle, every day here feels like a privilege.\r\n\r\nProperties offering this level of flexibility, space and breathtaking scenery are exceptionally rare. Whether you are searching for your forever home, a luxurious coastal retreat or a unique investment opportunity, this outstanding residence promises a lifestyle that is simply beyond comparison.\r\n\r\n***THIS PROPERTY IS NOT BER EXEMPT. BER REPORT WILL BE UPLOADED AS SOON AS IT BECOMES AVAILABLE.***"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Elevated 1-acre coastal site\r\nPanoramic Atlantic ocean views, including views of the Blasket Islands & Skellig Michael\r\nExceptional dual-living flexibility\r\nExtensive private parking & large steel garage/workshop\r\nPrime Wild Atlantic Way location on the Dingle Peninsula\r\nMinutes from Dunquin Pier & The Blasket Centre\r\nPeace & privacy, with breathtaking sunsets and coastal scenery\r\nClose to Slea Head Drive, Coumeenoole Beach & Dingle Way walking trails\r\nJust 20 kilometres from vibrant Dingle Town\r\nIdeal as a family home, holiday retreat or tourism investment"
      },
